    "sensesNotes": "Blindsight 30 ft in water",
    "tactics": "Jellyfish Swarms drift with currents until they encounter movement, warmth, or light. They surround swimmers and deckhands near the waterline, forcing characters to choose between taking the sting and leaving the water.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Stinging Tendrils: Opposed Reflex save using Agil 4 + Melee Combat 3 against every creature sharing the swarm's space. Target loses: 8 lightning damage and must make a Fortitude save with 1 success required or become Poisoned for 1 minute. Target wins: 4 lightning damage. At half HP or lower, deal 4 lightning damage on a loss and 2 lightning damage on a win; the Poisoned save still applies on a loss.</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Transparent Body: In clear water, ### Attacks against the Jellyfish Swarm add 1 to both dice unless the attacker is adjacent or using an area effect. Drifting Colony: The Jellyfish Swarm ignores difficult terrain caused by water currents and can move through spaces occupied by creatures. Swarm Body: The Jellyfish Swarm cannot be Grappled, Restrained, Prone, or Bleeding. Swarms: Swarms occupy a 5 × 5 ft space, halve physical damage, ignore Grappled, Restrained, Prone, and Bleeding, and resolve their ### Attacks as opposed Reflex saves. Each entry lists full damage and reduced damage once the swarm is at half HP or lower.</p>",
